    "answer": {
      "short": "$-17$. Multiply each fraction by its denominator's conjugate; the surd terms cancel.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4}{2+\\sqrt5}-\\frac{1}{9-4\\sqrt5}&=\\frac{4}{2+\\sqrt5}\\times\\frac{2-\\sqrt5}{2-\\sqrt5}-\\frac{1}{9-4\\sqrt5}\\times\\frac{9+4\\sqrt5}{9+4\\sqrt5}\\\\&=\\frac{8-4\\sqrt5}{4-5}-\\frac{9+4\\sqrt5}{81-80}\\\\&=-8+4\\sqrt5-9-4\\sqrt5\\\\&=-17\\end{align*}$$\nSince $-17$ is an integer, the expression is rational.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
